    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Vocabulary",
     "texto": [
      "In Portugal you say **autocarro** (bus) and in Brazil **ônibus**. **Comboio** (train) in Portugal and **trem** in Brazil. **Pequeno-almoço** (breakfast) in Portugal and **café da manhã** in Brazil. **Frigorífico** in Portugal, **geladeira** in Brazil. **Telemóvel** in Portugal, **celular** in Brazil."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Grammar",
     "texto": [
      "As a general trend, in Portugal **estou a fazer** is used a lot, and in Brazil **estou fazendo**. In European Portuguese, enclisis is common in simple affirmative sentences (**dou-te**), but elements that attract the pronoun cause proclisis; in Brazil proclisis is very common in speech.",
      "**Tu** and **você** depend on the region, the relationship between speakers and the register; they are not an absolute division between countries."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
